; ds4-blob-select-cli.fk -- stdin membrane for ds4-blob-select.fk.
;
; One root path in (the value of $HOME/models -- fkwu has no getenv door and cannot expand `~`
; itself, so the shell carrier reads the environment and hands the resolved root here, the same
; boundary native-model-route-table-cli.fk already keeps for $LOCAL_MODEL_ROUTE). The resolved DS4
; blob path -- or an honest empty one -- comes back as key=value lines, in the same discipline the
; shell already reads native-model-route-table-cli.fk's and native-model-event-cli.fk's output with
; (awk -F=). Which directories are asked, which architecture answers, and which of two look-alikes
; wins now live in ds4-blob-select.fk, not in a shell `[[ -f ]]` chain.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/ds4-blob-select.fk

(do
    (let root (read_line))
    (let blob (dbs-resolve root))
    (print_str (str_concat "ds4_blob_found=" (if (str_eq blob "") "0" "1")))
    (print_str (str_concat "ds4_blob_path=" blob)))
